### Tortoise - Event API
### Open in IntelliJ and click the green arrow next to each request.
### Restarting the app wipes everything (in-memory storage), so run them top to bottom.

@base = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Create an event -> 201 Created + Location header, status DRAFT
POST {{base}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Al Ahly vs Zamalek",
  "venue": "Cairo International Stadium",
  "totalSeats": 500,
  "registrationOpensAt": "2027-01-01T10:00:00Z",
  "registrationClosesAt": "2027-01-02T10:00:00Z",
  "eventStartsAt": "2027-01-10T19:00:00+02:00",
  "eventEndsAt": "2027-01-10T21:00:00+02:00"
}

### 2. Same name + venue + day (different letter case) -> 409 DUPLICATE_EVENT
POST {{base}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "AL AHLY VS ZAMALEK",
  "venue": "cairo international stadium",
  "totalSeats": 300,
  "registrationOpensAt": "2027-01-01T10:00:00Z",
  "registrationClosesAt": "2027-01-02T10:00:00Z",
  "eventStartsAt": "2027-01-10T15:00:00Z",
  "eventEndsAt": "2027-01-10T17:00:00Z"
}

### 3. Field validation -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED (totalSeats must be >= 1)
POST {{base}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Coding workshop",
  "venue": "Hall A",
  "totalSeats": 0,
  "registrationOpensAt": "2027-02-01T10:00:00Z",
  "registrationClosesAt": "2027-02-02T10:00:00Z",
  "eventStartsAt": "2027-02-10T10:00:00Z",
  "eventEndsAt": "2027-02-10T12:00:00Z"
}

### 4. Date rules -> 400 (registration must close 24h before start; end must be after start)
POST {{base}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Coding workshop",
  "venue": "Hall A",
  "totalSeats": 30,
  "registrationOpensAt": "2027-02-05T10:00:00Z",
  "registrationClosesAt": "2027-02-09T10:00:00Z",
  "eventStartsAt": "2027-02-09T19:00:00Z",
  "eventEndsAt": "2027-02-09T18:00:00Z"
}

### 5. Date in the past -> 400 "must be in the future"
POST {{base}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Old concert",
  "venue": "Opera House",
  "totalSeats": 100,
  "registrationOpensAt": "2020-01-01T10:00:00Z",
  "registrationClosesAt": "2027-02-02T10:00:00Z",
  "eventStartsAt": "2027-02-10T10:00:00Z",
  "eventEndsAt": "2027-02-10T12:00:00Z"
}

### 6. Malformed date -> 400 MALFORMED_REQUEST
POST {{base}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Coding workshop",
  "venue": "Hall A",
  "totalSeats": 30,
  "registrationOpensAt": "tomorrow"
}

### 7. Get one event -> 200
GET {{base}}/events/1

### 8. Event that doesn't exist -> 404 EVENT_NOT_FOUND
GET {{base}}/events/999

### 9. List with date filter and paging -> 200
GET {{base}}/events?from=2027-01-01&to=2027-01-31&page=0&size=5

### 10. No matches -> 200 with an empty list (not 404!)
GET {{base}}/events?from=2030-01-01

### 11. Bad paging -> 400
GET {{base}}/events?page=-1&size=500

### 12. Bad status value -> 400
GET {{base}}/events?status=banana

### 13. Edit a DRAFT event (any field) -> 200
PATCH {{base}}/events/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "totalSeats": 600,
  "description": "Derby day"
}
###
PATCH {{base}}/events/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "PUBLISHED"
}


### 14. Publish -> 200, status PUBLISHED
POST {{base}}/events/1/publish

### 15. Publish again -> 409 INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION
POST {{base}}/events/1/publish

### 16. Change seats after publishing -> 409 (only description may change)
PATCH {{base}}/events/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "totalSeats": 50
}

### 17. Change description after publishing -> 200
PATCH {{base}}/events/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Gates open at 5 PM"
}

### 18. Cancel (soft delete, data is kept) -> 200, status CANCELLED
POST {{base}}/events/1/cancel

### 19. Cancel again -> 409
POST {{base}}/events/1/cancel

### 20. There is no DELETE -> 405 METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED
DELETE {{base}}/events/1

### ---------- Review fixes (run after the requests above) ----------
### Note: the 409 in #2 still used up id 2, just like a database sequence skips a number
### when an insert fails. So the new "Derby" below gets id 3 and "Concert" gets id 4.

### 21. Create "Derby" again -> 201, id 3 (allowed: event 1 is CANCELLED, so the name is free again)
POST {{base}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Al Ahly vs Zamalek",
  "venue": "Cairo International Stadium",
  "totalSeats": 500,
  "registrationOpensAt": "2027-01-01T10:00:00Z",
  "registrationClosesAt": "2027-01-02T10:00:00Z",
  "eventStartsAt": "2027-01-10T19:00:00Z",
  "eventEndsAt": "2027-01-10T21:00:00Z"
}

### 22. Try to sneak a status change into PATCH -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED, hint to use /publish or /cancel
PATCH {{base}}/events/3
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "PUBLISHED"
}

### 23. Any unknown field is rejected, e.g. the typo "totalSeat" on create -> 400
POST {{base}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Concert",
  "venue": "Cairo International Stadium",
  "totalSeat": 100,
  "registrationOpensAt": "2027-01-01T10:00:00Z",
  "registrationClosesAt": "2027-01-02T10:00:00Z",
  "eventStartsAt": "2027-01-10T15:00:00Z",
  "eventEndsAt": "2027-01-10T17:00:00Z"
}

### 24. Create "Concert" at the same venue and day -> 201, id 4 (different name, no conflict)
POST {{base}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Concert",
  "venue": "Cairo International Stadium",
  "totalSeats": 100,
  "registrationOpensAt": "2027-01-01T10:00:00Z",
  "registrationClosesAt": "2027-01-02T10:00:00Z",
  "eventStartsAt": "2027-01-10T15:00:00Z",
  "eventEndsAt": "2027-01-10T17:00:00Z"
}

### 25. Rename "Concert" into "Derby" -> 409 DUPLICATE_EVENT
PATCH {{base}}/events/4
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "al ahly vs zamalek"
}

### 26. Change only the seats of "Derby" -> 200 (an event is never its own duplicate)
PATCH {{base}}/events/3
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "totalSeats": 900
}
